{"name":"Triassic","hex":"#67422d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Triassic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or from the geologic strata above the Permian and below the Jurassic; of or belonging to the period 250 to 200 million years ago when these strata were laid down."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A geologic period within the Mesozoic era, comprising lower, middle and upper epochs from about 250 to 200 million years ago."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Triassic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Triassic","blocks":[{"text":"The Triassic ( try-A-sik) is a geologic period and a stratigraphic system that spans 50.5 million years from the end of the Permian Period 251.902 Ma to the beginning of the Jurassic Period 201.4 Ma. The Triassic Period is the first and shortest geologic period of the Mesozoic Era, and the seventh period of the Phanerozoic Eon. The start and the end of the Triassic Period featured major extinction events."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Mollweide_Paleographic_Map_of_Earth%2C_225_Ma_%28Norian_Age%29.png/330px-Mollweide_Paleographic_Map_of_Earth%2C_225_Ma_%28Norian_Age%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triassic"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Stadtroda_Sandstein.jpg/250px-Stadtroda_Sandstein.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Stadtroda_Sandstein.jpg/330px-Stadtroda_Sandstein.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Stadtroda_Sandstein.jpg/250px-Stadtroda_Sandstein.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStadtroda_Sandstein.jpg"},{"srcs